 look into the CSP  exam requirements the primary  requirement for any candidate is that  they should have at least five years of  work experience in the field of  information security in addition to this  it is also suggested that the candidate  clears our  certifications like CCNA CompTIA  security plus CH CS m and C is a to name  a few  CS SP is considered as an advanced level  cybersecurity certification hence it is  better if the candidate clears the basic  level and the managerial level  certifications before moving to the CSP  certification as I mentioned earlier  this certification is suitable for  professionals who have a minimum of five  years of work experience professionals  working as security consultants and  managers Network and security architects  IT directors security auditors and chief  information security officers can take  up the CSP certification now let's move  on and understand more about the CISSP  exam this certification is developed by  the international information system  security certification consortium is  e-square the certificate provider is IC  square you have to pay an exam fee of  699 dollars to take up this exam as I  mentioned earlier this is one of the  toughest exams and it is quite a long  one with a duration of six SARS  you would have to answer 250 questions  in six hours the exam consists of  multiple choice questions you need to be  able to get a minimum score of 700 out  of thousand for passing the CSP exam  let's now move on to our next topic that  is cissp domains this entire  certification is grouped into a total of  eight domains the broad spectrum of  topics included in CS SP ensure its  relevance across all disciplines in the  fields of information security  successful candidates are competent in  the following eight domains they are  security and risk management then we  have asset security security engineering  communications and network security  followed by identity and access  management then security assessm